35,2,1,talk,Mio,,The ledger shows fixed costs are huge. Bank statements show many late payments.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The sign-in sheets show a quarter of people do two-thirds of the work.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Takumi,,The rota confirms the same nine people do the setup. It is unfair.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,Chasing individual payments takes six hours a month. Yearly collection is easier.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,Taster forms say people fear a whole year commitment. Winter social shows anxiety.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, if yearly collection is easier, maybe we should go back to that?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Takumi, if the work is so uneven, a flat fee feels wrong to me.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Mio, a flat fee ignores the fact that some people barely come.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,I prefer a structure that minimizes administrative burden. Flat or tiered?,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Jonathan, if people are hesitant, maybe activity-based charging feels less scary?","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,Activity-based charging might scare people off if they think it is expensive per event.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I worry that activity-based charging makes people feel like guests, not members.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"Tiered membership could let heavy users pay more, but it might create cliques.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,Tiered membership adds complexity. Flat fee is simplest for the books.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,I think a small base fee plus event charges might be the most flexible.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
